  "preamble": "Middle Chinese voiced stops became voiceless aspirated stops in much of Sinitic, so that the voiced velar [ɡ] surfaces as [kʰ]. In Hakka and Gan the change applied in every tone, while in Mandarin and Cantonese it depends on tone: Mandarin aspirates only level-tone syllables, and in both, departing-tone syllables such as 共 keep unaspirated [k]. Independently, Western Armenian turned the Classical Armenian voiced series into voiceless aspirates, so Classical գ /ɡ/ is Western Armenian [kʰ].",
